# L §5.10 Value: the price `by p` names is "an input or def of type `num CUR/u`"; read through its carry, `by
# last(px)`.  val is an unkeyed `money PLN reading`, a value and not a price per unit, so `by last(val)` is refused at
# load as a price of the wrong type (LOAD-UNIT), as a price written as an expression of the wrong type is.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit etf "fund unit"

kind funds: place etf min 0

input val: money PLN reading

place fund: funds lives 2026-01-01..

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  val = 12.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 "kurs"

ask q1: value(fund, 2026-06-30) in PLN by last(val)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT value by last(val): the price is money PLN, not num PLN/u (m.tally:23)
